From ae8d20cfddcc2d40104b73ff59abec68946d242d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SlippyGetBackHere <343265862+SlippyGetBackHere@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:44:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] host: a modal choice list a title's own code can open

snes_choice_menu_open(title, items, count, initial, cancel_allowed,
done, user) arms a "pick one" list (up to 16 items). The host notices
at the next frame boundary and runs it like the save-state browser:
the guest stays frozen, audio pauses, the list is drawn centred over the
frozen picture, and `done` runs at that boundary with the choice (or -1
when cancelled), so it may change guest RAM. Controls are the player's
own bindings and pad: Up/Down move; A, B or Start choose; Y cancels;
Enter/Space and Escape too. SNESRECOMP_CHOICE_MENU_AUTO=<index> answers
it for headless runs. A game's stage select mod uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
